---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const archives = [
  {
    title: "Designr.link",
    period: "2014–2018",
    kind: "Selected work",
    description: "Product, public-service, interactive and game design across teams, continents and formats.",
    href: "/archive/designr/index.html",
    variant: "designr",
  },
  {
    title: "Design Sans Frontières",
    period: "2009–2014",
    kind: "Personal archive",
    description: "Design, games, photography, wanderlust and beautifully geeky things from an earlier internet.",
    href: "/archive/design-sans-frontieres/index.html",
    variant: "sans-frontieres",
  },
  {
    title: "Berlin 3.0",
    period: "2012–2013",
    kind: "Field dispatches",
    description: "Thirty-two dispatches from Berlin School, travelling Berlin → Shanghai → Tokyo → New York.",
    href: "/archive/berlin-3/index.html",
    variant: "berlin",
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="About | Vivid Savitri-Hampton"
  description="How I got here: HCI and industrial design, two startup exits, then agent systems and local AI operating systems deployed at Breville. Sydney, Australia."
  pathname="/about/"
>
  <article class="container-wide pt-16 pb-24" style="max-width: 1400px;">

    <div class="about-header">
      <div class="about-intro">
        <p class="small-caps mb-8">About</p>
        <h1 class="mb-8">
          The tools will continue to change, but the question of who this system fails on doesn't.
        </h1>
      </div>
      <div class="about-portrait-wrap">
        <img
          src="/vivid-portrait.webp"
          alt="Vivid Savitri-Hampton"
          class="about-portrait"
          width="200"
          height="200"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-body">
      <p>
        My name is Vivid, I'm an Applied AI Product Engineer based in Sydney. I build
        agent systems, local AI operating systems, and the governance scaffolding that
        lets other people run them.
      </p>

      <p>
        I came to this from HCI and industrial design, where you cannot patch a product
        after it ships, so you learn early to ask who it fails on. I have been asking
        that same question ever since, even as the substrate keeps changing underneath
        me: physical products first, then video games, then AI.
      </p>

      <p>
        Most recently the question took me to Breville, where I prototyped the company's
        first Model Context Protocol (MCP) tool in July 2024: a custom GPT sitting over more than
        235,000 brand assets, now in production with the BRG engineering team. Before
        that there were two startup exits in video games, one out of Shanghai and another
        while in Berlin, and a long stretch of living and working across twelve countries
        on four continents. Somewhere in the middle of it I did AI Product Management at
        Duke and an MBA at Steinbeis Hochschule Berlin, where my thesis was on AI-driven
        experience design.
      </p>

      <h2>What I work on</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Agentic AI systems</strong>: multi-agent architectures with explicit
          safety envelopes, LLM orchestration, evaluation harnesses
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Local AI operating systems</strong>: enterprise agentic environments
          with governance scaffolding, policy controls, and safety gates built into the
          runtime. <a href="https://cowork-os.netlify.app/coworkos-setup-guide-personal-20260818" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CoworkOS (Claude Cowork)</a> and WorkspaceOS (Codex) deployed at Breville;
          <a href="https://cowork-os.netlify.app/kimios-setup-guide" target="_blank" rel="noopener">KimiOS (Kimi Work)</a> for personal use, integrating a Karpathy-style second brain
          for longitudinal reasoning
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Privacy-first AI infrastructure</strong>: provenance-aware retrieval,
          longitudinal reasoning scaffolds, human-in-the-loop review gates
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Human-AI interaction</strong>: designing experiences where AI augments
          decision-making instead of obscuring it
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why I care about safety</h2>

      <p>
        Most AI demos look good on happy-path prompts and fall apart the moment you ask
        the hard questions: provenance, override, longitudinal change, failure modes.
      </p>

      <p>
        That's what threads my work together: <a href="/projects/vai-sante-os/">multimodal
        memory with chain-of-custody</a>, <a href="/projects/vivid-alpaca/">multi-agent
        trading with execution guardrails</a>, <a href="/projects/espresso-horoscope-mcp/">local
        agents with strict tool boundaries</a>. The use cases may differ, but the discipline doesn't.
      </p>

      <h2>Currently building</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>
          An AI-enabled video game, still in stealth
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://koinaku.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Koinaku</a>, a
          financial literacy app for the next generation of Indonesians, currently in
          early beta
        </li>
        <li>
          Hybrid model routing across local models (LM Studio) and OpenRouter-hosted
          models, including Qwen 3.x variants
        </li>
        <li>
          AI evaluation frameworks aimed at product decisions, not benchmark gaming
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Accolades</h2>

      <p>
        The AI work is the project list further up this page, so what follows is the decade
        before it: physical products that shipped and sold in real volume, plus a few
        hackathon results from back when AI still mostly meant a chatbot.
      </p>

      <h3>Product design</h3>

      <ul>
        <li>Red Dot Award 2022, Best of the Best: Breville Barista Express Impress BES876</li>
        <li>SCA Award 2022: Breville Barista Express Impress BES876</li>
        <li>Good Design Award 2022: Breville Joule Oven Air Pro</li>
        <li>Red Dot Award 2020: Breville Polyscience HydroPro SousVide</li>
        <li>Red Dot Award 2020: Breville Nespresso Creatista Pro</li>
        <li>IDSA 2019, Bronze: Breville Smart Oven AirFry</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Software and data</h3>

      <ul>
        <li>NASA SpaceApps 2017, 1st Place Australia / Top 25 Global</li>
        <li>NASA SpaceApps 2016, 1st Place Australia / Top 5 Global</li>
        <li>Chatfuel Chatbot 2017, Top 10 Global Finalist: Stake Chatbot</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Academia</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>Adjunct Associate Lecturer, University of New South Wales, Australia (School of Biotechnology & Biomolecular Sciences, Faculty of Science) (2023-2025)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Education</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>Entrepreneurial Studies, Stanford Graduate School of Business (2024)</li>
        <li>AI Product Management, Duke University (Pratt School of Engineering) (2023)</li>
        <li>MBA, Steinbeis Hochschule Berlin (Thesis: AI-Driven Application for Experience Design) (2019)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Languages</h2>
      <p>English · French · Mandarin</p>

      <h2>Reach out</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="mailto:hello@veryvivid.xyz">hello (at) veryvivid.xyz</a> ·
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/vnsavitri/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a> ·
        <a href="https://github.com/vnsavitri" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a> ·
        <a href="mailto:vnsavitri@protonmail.ch">Email</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="archive-divider"></div>

    <div class="container-wide archive-section" id="archives">
      <div class="archive-header">
        <div>
          <p class="small-caps archive-kicker">Past lives / preserved work</p>
          <h2>Archive</h2>
        </div>
        <span class="small-caps">Three snapshots</span>
      </div>

      <div class="archive-grid">
        {archives.map((archive) => (
          <a
            href={archive.href}
            class={`archive-card archive-card-${archive.variant}`}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
          >
            <div class="archive-preview" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="archive-preview-index">{archive.period}</span>
              <span class="archive-preview-title">{archive.title}</span>
              <span class="archive-preview-rule"></span>
              <span class="archive-preview-label">ARCHIVED / OPEN</span>
            </div>
            <div class="archive-card-body">
              <div class="archive-meta small-caps">
                <span>{archive.period}</span>
                <span>{archive.kind}</span>
              </div>
              <h3>{archive.title}</h3>
              <p>{archive.description}</p>
              <span class="archive-cta">Open archive →</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>

      <p class="archive-note">
        Earlier work, preserved as standalone sites. The archives open in a new tab so this portfolio remains your wayfinding layer.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-header {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    gap: 5rem;
    align-items: start;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .about-portrait {
    width: 200px;
    height: 200px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: 50% 15%;
    display: block;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .about-header {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
    }

    .about-portrait {
      width: 140px;
      height: 140px;
    }
  }

  /* Archive cards: the small preview borrows each site's visual language without
     pulling its large media libraries into the main portfolio. */
  .archive-divider {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    margin-top: 4rem;
  }

  .archive-section {
    padding-top: 4rem;
  }

  .archive-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .archive-kicker {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .archive-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }

  .archive-card {
    display: flex;
    min-width: 0;
    flex-direction: column;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-cream) 74%, white);
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: border-color 0.2s ease, transform 0.2s ease, background 0.2s ease;
  }

  .archive-card:hover,
  .archive-card:focus-visible {
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
    background: var(--color-cream);
    transform: translateY(-3px);
  }

  .archive-preview {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    min-height: 11rem;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    overflow: hidden;
    padding: 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    background: var(--archive-ink);
    color: var(--archive-paper);
  }

  .archive-preview::before,
  .archive-preview::after {
    position: absolute;
    content: "";
  }

  .archive-preview::before {
    width: 5.5rem;
    height: 5.5rem;
    right: -1.25rem;
    top: -1.25rem;
    background: var(--archive-accent);
  }

  .archive-preview::after {
    width: 3.5rem;
    height: 3.5rem;
    right: 2rem;
    bottom: -1.25rem;
    background: var(--archive-secondary);
  }

  .archive-preview-index,
  .archive-preview-label {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .archive-preview-title {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    max-width: 9ch;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 2.8vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.06em;
    line-height: 0.9;
  }

  .archive-preview-rule {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 1;
    right: 1rem;
    bottom: 1rem;
    left: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--archive-paper) 35%, transparent);
  }

  .archive-card-designr {
    --archive-ink: #1a1a1a;
    --archive-paper: #f5f3ee;
    --archive-accent: #c23a2c;
    --archive-secondary: #f0c808;
  }

  .archive-card-sans-frontieres {
    --archive-ink: #0057b8;
    --archive-paper: #fafafa;
    --archive-accent: #e63227;
    --archive-secondary: #1a1a1a;
  }

  .archive-card-berlin {
    --archive-ink: #1b1a17;
    --archive-paper: #e4e1d9;
    --archive-accent: #a8371e;
    --archive-secondary: #d6d2c7;
  }

  .archive-card-body {
    display: flex;
    flex: 1;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }

  .archive-meta {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .archive-meta span:last-child {
    text-align: right;
  }

  .archive-card h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    transition: color 0.15s ease;
  }

  .archive-card:hover h3,
  .archive-card:focus-visible h3 {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .archive-card p {
    flex: 1;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }

  .archive-cta {
    align-self: flex-start;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    padding-bottom: 2px;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  .archive-card:hover .archive-cta,
  .archive-card:focus-visible .archive-cta {
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .archive-note {
    max-width: 65ch;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .archive-card {
      transition: border-color 0.2s ease, background 0.2s ease;
    }

    .archive-card:hover,
    .archive-card:focus-visible {
      transform: none;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .archive-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .archive-card {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(12rem, 0.8fr) 1fr;
    }

    .archive-preview {
      min-height: 100%;
      border-right: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
      border-bottom: 0;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .archive-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .archive-card {
      display: flex;
    }

    .archive-preview {
      min-height: 10rem;
      border-right: 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    }
  }
</style>
